   Correct, nu'o would be a bad idea for that reason.  It does mean that you
have never yet believed, whereas atheists might have been theists sometime
in their past.   It also eliminate those hypothetical atheists who are not
innately capable of being theists (remember, nu'o means "can, but hasn't").

  I also think that stylistically, "na" is a bad thing to use in all lujvo,
since it has bridi-wide implications.

  Also, not real fond of "nalceikri" for atheist.  A "nalceikri" would
logically be a non-theist, and include agnostics.  An atheist would be a
"tolceikri"
             --gejyspa


